{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:18:13Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 84, "kind": "message", "text": "No lint/type-check config exists for the backend \u2014 `pytest` is the only verification command, and it passes. Implementation is complete.\n\n## Handoff\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 `TaskStore.__init__` now resolves a data-file path from `TASKS_DATA_FILE` env var (default `backend/data/tasks.json`, relative to `store.py`'s own location) and calls a new `_load()` on construction. `_load()` reads+parses the file and validates each entry against `Task`; any exception (missing file, bad JSON, wrong shape) is caught and the store starts empty \u2014 matches AC5/AC6, one code path for both. `_next_id` becomes `max(loaded ids, default=0) + 1`. Added `_save()` \u2014 creates the parent dir (`mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)`, AC7) and writes the full task list as JSON. Called at the end of every mutating method: `add`, `set_done`, `set_priority`, `update_title`, `delete` (only on actual removal), `reset`.\n- `backend/tests/conftest.py` \u2014 sets `TASKS_DATA_FILE` to a fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp()` path before `app.main` is imported, so the module-level `store` singleton never touches the real data file (AC8). Verified: no `backend/data/` directory exists after running the suite.\n- `backend/tests/test_persistence.py` (new) \u2014 8 tests: restart survival (two `TaskStore` instances, same path), missing file, corrupt JSON, wrong top-level shape (object not array), wrong item shape, empty file, id-counter continuation after non-contiguous deletes, and directory auto-creation.\n\n**Not changed:** `backend/app/main.py`, `backend/app/models.py`, `frontend/` \u2014 as the spec/design predicted, persistence is fully transparent to routes.\n\n**One thing I could not do:** the spec's \"Affected areas\" calls for adding `backend/data/` to `.gitignore`. I don't have write permission to `.gitignore` in this sandbox (the `Edit` call was denied twice). Someone with permission needs to add:\n```\nbackend/data/\n```\nWithout it, a real run's `backend/data/tasks.json` risks being `git add`-ed accidentally.\n\n**Verification run this session:**\n```\ncd backend && python3 -m pytest -q\n# 30 passed (22 pre-existing + 8 new), 0.11s\n```\nI could not start `uvicorn` to do a live curl-based restart check (background Bash execution was denied in this sandbox), so the restart behavior is verified via `test_persistence.py`'s two-`TaskStore`-instances-same-path tests rather than an actual process restart \u2014 this is the same technique used to test the store in isolation elsewhere in this suite (constructing `TaskStore()` directly rather than going through `app`).\n\n**Deviations from spec:** none. All 8 acceptance criteria are covered by the new tests; non-goals (no DB, no file locking, no partial recovery, no export endpoint, no frontend change) were respected.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "609b1f52-83bc-4e30-8fbc-2d3e3a5d7719"}}
